{"title": "Designing a permission system", "kind": "Worked example", "weight": "Landmark", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "definition": null, "facts": [{"text": "An access control list (ACL) is a list of rules that specifies which users are granted or denied access to a particular resource.", "sent_ids": ["e37197ac497e"]}, {"text": "ACL is easy to understand, but it is error-prone and its maintenance cost is high.", "sent_ids": ["7f9d58a57b50", "ce6ce76575cf"]}, {"text": "Discretionary access control (DAC) is based on ACL: it grants or restricts object access through an access policy determined by the object's owner group.", "sent_ids": ["eca74d964163", "be8fda8590f4"]}, {"text": "DAC is easy and flexible, and the Linux file system supports it, but permission control is scattered and the object's owner group has too much power.", "sent_ids": ["abc7995a68d3", "ddeaae199142", "73aea0fd5ca8"]}, {"text": "In mandatory access control (MAC) both resource owners and resources have classification labels, and different labels are granted different permissions.", "sent_ids": ["e4f5c258641b", "9aac8d36dd10"]}, {"text": "MAC is strict and straightforward, but not flexible.", "sent_ids": ["192b324a420d", "1ed2032175fe"]}, {"text": "Attribute-based access control (ABAC) evaluates permissions based on attributes of the resource owner, the action, the resource and the environment.", "sent_ids": ["8310f1b68851"]}, {"text": "ABAC is flexible, but its rules can be complicated and the implementation is hard; it is not commonly used.", "sent_ids": ["bdb1ec63f6f0", "2ea14eea94ea", "ae72dcd324a9"]}, {"text": "Role-based access control (RBAC) evaluates permissions based on roles, and is flexible in assigning roles.", "sent_ids": ["e163d58c1340", "2418c5e29ada"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-reliab-030", "sysd-reliab-031", "sysd-q-010", "sysd-q-014", "sysd-q-013"], "related": ["sysd-q-011", "sysd-q-012", "sysd-reliab-015"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": [], "wants_image": false, "notes": "thin: the guide only lists five access-control models with pros and cons; no requirements, scale, data model, API, policy engine, or advice on which model to choose.", "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-009", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "curated", "curriculum": ["own article", "question entry"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["e37197ac497e", "7f9d58a57b50", "ce6ce76575cf", "eca74d964163", "be8fda8590f4", "abc7995a68d3", "ddeaae199142", "73aea0fd5ca8", "e4f5c258641b", "9aac8d36dd10", "192b324a420d", "1ed2032175fe", "8310f1b68851", "bdb1ec63f6f0", "2ea14eea94ea", "ae72dcd324a9", "e163d58c1340", "2418c5e29ada"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
{"title": "Access control list", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Foundational", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md#1. ACL (Access Control List)", "definition": {"text": "A list of rules that specifies which users are granted or denied access to a particular resource.", "sent_ids": ["e37197ac497e"]}, "facts": [{"text": "An ACL is a list of rules that specifies which users are granted or denied access to a particular resource.", "sent_ids": ["e37197ac497e"]}, {"text": "An access policy can be expressed as an access control list.", "sent_ids": ["f9b5ace6bfa1"]}, {"text": "ACLs are easy to understand, but they are error-prone and their maintenance cost is high.", "sent_ids": ["7f9d58a57b50", "ce6ce76575cf"]}, {"text": "Even when access is controlled by authentication plus access control lists, maintaining the authorization data is not trivial and often costs as much administration as managing authentication credentials.", "sent_ids": ["e9e555005cfb"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-reliab-030"], "related": ["sysd-q-011", "sysd-q-014"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Discretionary access control", "Mandatory access control", "Attribute-based access control", "Role-based access control"], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-010", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "reference", "curriculum": ["own section", "mentioned on 2+ pages"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["e37197ac497e", "7f9d58a57b50", "ce6ce76575cf"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}, {"title": "Authorization", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authorization", "revid": 1341431660, "sent_ids": ["f9b5ace6bfa1", "e9e555005cfb"], "key": "Authorization", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1341431660"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
{"title": "Discretionary access control", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md#2. DAC (Discretionary Access Control)", "definition": {"text": "An access-control model, built on ACLs, in which an access policy determined by the object's owner group grants or restricts access to the object.", "sent_ids": ["eca74d964163", "be8fda8590f4"]}, "facts": [{"text": "DAC is based on ACL and grants or restricts object access through an access policy determined by the object's owner group.", "sent_ids": ["eca74d964163", "be8fda8590f4"]}, {"text": "DAC is easy and flexible, and the Linux file system supports it.", "sent_ids": ["abc7995a68d3", "ddeaae199142"]}, {"text": "Its drawbacks are scattered permission control and too much power for the object's owner group.", "sent_ids": ["73aea0fd5ca8"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-q-010"], "related": ["sysd-q-012"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Access control list", "Mandatory access control", "Attribute-based access control", "Role-based access control"], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-011", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "curated", "curriculum": ["own section"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["eca74d964163", "be8fda8590f4", "abc7995a68d3", "ddeaae199142", "73aea0fd5ca8"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
{"title": "Mandatory access control", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md#3. MAC (Mandatory Access Control)", "definition": {"text": "An access-control model in which resource owners and resources carry classification labels, and each label is granted its own permissions.", "sent_ids": ["e4f5c258641b", "9aac8d36dd10"]}, "facts": [{"text": "In MAC both resource owners and resources have classification labels, and different labels are granted different permissions.", "sent_ids": ["e4f5c258641b", "9aac8d36dd10"]}, {"text": "MAC is strict and straightforward.", "sent_ids": ["192b324a420d"]}, {"text": "MAC is not flexible.", "sent_ids": ["1ed2032175fe"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-reliab-030"], "related": ["sysd-q-011"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Access control list", "Discretionary access control", "Attribute-based access control", "Role-based access control"], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-012", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "curated", "curriculum": ["own section"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["e4f5c258641b", "9aac8d36dd10", "192b324a420d", "1ed2032175fe"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
{"title": "Attribute-based access control", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Minor", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md#4. ABAC (Attribute-based access control)", "definition": {"text": "An access-control model that evaluates permissions from attributes of the resource owner, the action, the resource and the environment.", "sent_ids": ["8310f1b68851"]}, "facts": [{"text": "ABAC evaluates permissions based on attributes of the resource owner, the action, the resource and the environment.", "sent_ids": ["8310f1b68851"]}, {"text": "ABAC is flexible.", "sent_ids": ["bdb1ec63f6f0"]}, {"text": "Its rules can be complicated and the implementation is hard, so it is not commonly used.", "sent_ids": ["2ea14eea94ea", "ae72dcd324a9"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-reliab-030"], "related": ["sysd-q-014"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Access control list", "Discretionary access control", "Mandatory access control", "Role-based access control"], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-013", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "curated", "curriculum": ["own section"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["8310f1b68851", "bdb1ec63f6f0", "2ea14eea94ea", "ae72dcd324a9"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
{"title": "Role-based access control", "kind": "Concept", "weight": "Major", "level": "Intermediate", "article": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md#5. RBAC (Role-based Access Control)", "definition": {"text": "An access-control model that evaluates permissions from the roles a subject has been granted.", "sent_ids": ["e163d58c1340", "4c50ab080594"]}, "facts": [{"text": "RBAC evaluates permissions based on roles: subjects are granted one or more roles, and the resource being accessed is checked for having been assigned at least one of those roles. It is a widely used model in modern systems.", "sent_ids": ["e163d58c1340", "4c50ab080594"]}, {"text": "RBAC is flexible in assigning roles.", "sent_ids": ["2418c5e29ada"]}, {"text": "In Kubernetes' RBAC mode, access rights are granted to users based on the roles granted to them, and each role defines a list of allowed actions.", "sent_ids": ["741ed86827d2"]}], "prerequisites": ["sysd-reliab-030"], "related": ["sysd-q-010", "sysd-q-013"], "contested": false, "contested_note": null, "conflicts": [], "distinct_from": ["Access control list", "Discretionary access control", "Mandatory access control", "Attribute-based access control"], "wants_image": false, "notes": null, "part": "Design interview questions", "chapter": "Design a permission system", "id": "sysd-q-014", "verification": [], "external": [], "source_tier": "reference", "curriculum": ["own section", "mentioned on 2+ pages"], "sources": [{"title": "how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md (ByteByteGo System Design 101)", "url": "https://github.com/ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/blob/b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "revid": null, "sent_ids": ["e163d58c1340", "2418c5e29ada"], "key": "gh>ByteByteGoHq/system-design-101/data/guides/how-do-we-design-a-permission-system.md", "source": "bytebytego-101", "version": "b28380a4710c5ec9638ec037d4168e288f334cba", "license": {"name": "CC BY-NC-ND 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/", "class": "cc-by-nc-nd", "verified": "2026-11-18", "evidence": "LICENSE.md: 'This work is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0'"}}, {"title": "Authorization", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authorization", "revid": 1341431660, "sent_ids": ["4c50ab080594"], "key": "Authorization", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1341431660"}, {"title": "Kubernetes", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubernetes", "revid": 1384303361, "sent_ids": ["741ed86827d2"], "key": "Kubernetes", "source": "wikipedia", "version": "1384303361"}], "events": [], "flags": [], "qid": null}
